  "label": "User projected onto the person shoveling snow",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the person shoveling snow, as indicated by the text 'i hate snow' which uses the first-person pronoun 'i'. This creates an analogical mapping where the person in the image is implicitly identified as 'me' — the speaker of the text. The user sees themselves in the role of the person performing the laborious task of snow removal, thereby projecting their own experience or attitude onto the visual subject.",
